1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:02,999
MyCampusView Academy.

2
00:00:03,049 --> 00:00:05,565
Robotics 101, video 5.

3
00:00:05,615 --> 00:00:09,880
How motors and the motor driver work.

4
00:00:11,050 --> 00:00:14,516
Our robot has two motors, one for each wheel.

5
00:00:14,566 --> 00:00:19,360
Let us see how the Arduino controls their direction and speed.

6
00:00:20,750 --> 00:00:24,871
Inside the L298N are switches arranged like the letter H.

7
00:00:24,921 --> 00:00:26,847
That is called an H-bridge.

8
00:00:26,897 --> 00:00:31,970
Two control pins decide which way the current flows through the motor.

9
00:00:33,350 --> 00:00:38,509
If IN1 is HIGH and IN2 is LOW, the motor spins forward.

10
00:00:38,559 --> 00:00:41,635
Swap them, and it spins backward.

11
00:00:41,685 --> 00:00:44,760
If both are LOW, the motor stops.

12
00:00:46,150 --> 00:00:49,394
The enable pin sets the speed.

13
00:00:49,444 --> 00:00:54,334
The Arduino switches it on and off very fast.

14
00:00:54,384 --> 00:00:56,420
This is called PWM.

15
00:00:56,470 --> 00:00:59,824
On most of the time means fast.

16
00:00:59,874 --> 00:01:04,215
On only a little of the time means slow.

17
00:01:04,265 --> 00:01:06,960
Speed goes from 0 to 255.

18
00:01:08,350 --> 00:01:11,218
Our robot has no steering wheel.

19
00:01:11,268 --> 00:01:15,868
It turns by driving its wheels at different speeds.

20
00:01:15,918 --> 00:01:19,789
Both wheels the same speed: straight ahead.

21
00:01:19,839 --> 00:01:23,527
Left wheel slower: the robot curves left.

22
00:01:23,577 --> 00:01:26,810
Right wheel slower: it curves right.

23
00:01:28,150 --> 00:01:31,859
Watch the left and right motor numbers on the panel.

24
00:01:31,909 --> 00:01:36,341
When the line curves, one wheel slows down and the robot turns

25
00:01:36,391 --> 00:01:37,570
towards the line.

26
00:01:43,300 --> 00:01:44,587
Let us recap.

27
00:01:44,637 --> 00:01:46,849
IN pins set direction.

28
00:01:46,899 --> 00:01:49,625
EN pins set speed with PWM.

29
00:01:49,675 --> 00:01:53,635
Different wheel speeds steer the robot.

30
00:01:53,685 --> 00:01:56,720
Next: Building the robot body.
